        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:07:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1074,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 1090,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 151291,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 18,
        "headingId": 1090,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:07:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1075,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 1091,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 151292,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 18,
        "headingId": 1091,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The labium majus is the most common site of occurrence {25357118}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:07:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1076,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 1092,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 151293,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 18,
        "headingId": 1092,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients present with a vulvar mass that may be rapidly growing {20035149; 25357118; 23354802; 21293278}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:07:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1077,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 1093,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 151294,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 18,
        "headingId": 1093,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These are very uncommon vulvar neoplasms. The average patient age at presentation is 39&nbsp;years (range: 17&ndash;69&nbsp;years) {20035149; 25357118; 23354802; 21293278}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:07:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1078,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 1094,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 151295,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 18,
        "headingId": 1094,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:07:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1079,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 1095,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 151296,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 18,
        "headingId": 1095,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These are thought to arise from anogenital mammary-like glands. Proliferative lesions of the anogenital mammary-like glands have been reported in the setting of germline <em>PTEN</em> mutation (Cowden syndrome) {27090873; 33850997}. The only reported genomic study analysed 2&nbsp;low-grade vulvar phyllodes tumours, one of which showed mutations involving <em>ABL1</em> and <em>TP53</em> genes {28648934}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:07:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1086,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 1102,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 151297,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 18,
        "headingId": 1102,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These are variably circumscribed masses with a solid or solid and cystic cut surface. Leaf-like structures may be evident grossly. The average size is 33&nbsp;mm (range: 7&ndash;66&nbsp;mm) {20035149; 25357118; 23354802; 21293278}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:07:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1080,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 1096,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 151298,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 18,
        "headingId": 1096,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Phyllodes tumours contain bland glandular elements lined by mammary-like epithelium, with a prominent leaf-like stromal growth protruding into the glandular lumina. They typically display regional variability in stromal cellularity, with band-like areas of hypercellularity and increased mitotic activity around the epithelial components (periglandular cuffing). Phyllodes tumours are classified as benign, borderline, or malignant types; it is recommended that similar criteria be used as are used in the breast {26768026}. See the WHO classification of breast tumours [[WHO Classification of Tumours Editorial Board. Breast tumours. Lyon (France): International Agency for Research on Cancer; forthcoming. (WHO classification of tumours series, 6th ed.; vol. 2). https://publications.iarc.who.int.]].</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:07:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1081,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 1097,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 151299,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 18,
        "headingId": 1097,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The cytopathology features for vulvar phyllodes tumour have not yet been documented in the cytopathology literature.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:07:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1082,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 1098,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 151300,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 18,
        "headingId": 1098,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:07:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1085,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 1101,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 151301,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 18,
        "headingId": 1101,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> biphasic histology; mammary-like epithelium with a prominent leaf-like architecture; hypercellular stroma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:07:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1083,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 1099,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 151302,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 18,
        "headingId": 1099,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Because the stromal component of phyllodes tumours represents the neoplastic component, malignant phyllodes tumours may be staged as sarcomas using the ninth edition of the Union for International Cancer Control (UICC) TNM classification [[Brierley JD, Giuliani M, O&rsquo;Sullivan B, et al., editors. TNM Classification of Malignant Tumours. 9th ed. Oxford (UK): John Wiley &amp; Sons; 2025.]].</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:07:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1084,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 1100,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 151303,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 18,
        "headingId": 1100,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Approximately 20% of reported cases have recurred locally, including some histologically benign tumours. There have been no reported cases of distant metastases {20035149; 25357118}. It is recommended that similar criteria be used to predict malignant behaviour as are used in the breast; however, because these are uncommon vulvar neoplasms, the criteria predicting malignant behaviour are not well established {26768026}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:07:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]